#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:1
msgid "Supported Array Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:3
msgid ""
"PyGMT uses NumPy arrays as its core data structure for storing data and "
"exchanging data with the GMT C API. This design allows PyGMT to support a "
"wide range of array-like objects and data types (*dtypes*), as long as they "
"can be converted to NumPy arrays. This page provides a comprehensive "
"overview of the array dtypes supported by PyGMT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:8
msgid "Numeric Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:10
msgid ""
"In addition to Python's built-in numeric types ({class}`int` and {class}"
"`float`), PyGMT supports most of the numeric dtypes provided by NumPy, "
"pandas, and PyArrow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:13
msgid "**Signed Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:15
msgid ""
"`numpy.int8`, `numpy.int16`, `numpy.int32`, `numpy.int64`, {class}`numpy."
"longlong`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:16
msgid ""
"{class}`pandas.Int8Dtype`, {class}`pandas.Int16Dtype`, {class}`pandas."
"Int32Dtype`, {class}`pandas.Int64Dtype`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:18
msgid ""
"{func}`pyarrow.int8`, {func}`pyarrow.int16`, {func}`pyarrow.int32`, {func}"
"`pyarrow.int64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:21
msgid "**Unsigned Integers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:23
msgid ""
"`numpy.uint8`, `numpy.uint16`, `numpy.uint32`, `numpy.uint64`, {class}`numpy."
"ulonglong`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:24
msgid ""
"{class}`pandas.UInt8Dtype`, {class}`pandas.UInt16Dtype`, {class}`pandas."
"UInt32Dtype`, {class}`pandas.UInt64Dtype`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:26
msgid ""
"{func}`pyarrow.uint8`, {func}`pyarrow.uint16`, {func}`pyarrow.uint32`, {func}"
"`pyarrow.uint64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:29
msgid "**Floating-point numbers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:31
msgid "`numpy.float32`, `numpy.float64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:32
msgid "{class}`pandas.Float32Dtype`, {class}`pandas.Float64Dtype`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:33
msgid "{func}`pyarrow.float32`, {func}`pyarrow.float64`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:36
msgid ""
"Signed and unsigned integer dtypes from pandas and PyArrow (e.g., {class}"
"`pandas.Int8Dtype`, {func}`pyarrow.int8`) support missing values like `None` "
"or {class}`pandas.NA`, whereas NumPy's corresponding dtypes (e.g., `numpy."
"int8`) don't. Arrays of these dtypes containing missing values are "
"automatically cast to `numpy.float64` internally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:41
msgid ""
"For 3-D {class}`xarray.DataArray` objects representing raster images, only 8-"
"bit unsigned integers (i.e., `numpy.uint8`) are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:46
msgid "Examples of numeric arrays supported by PyGMT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:48
msgid ""
"# A list of integers\n"
"[1, 2, 3]\n"
"\n"
"# A NumPy array with dtype int32\n"
"np.array([1, 2, 3], dtype=np.int32)\n"
"\n"
"# A pandas Series with nullable Int32 dtype\n"
"pd.Series([1, 2, 3], dtype=\"Int32\")\n"
"\n"
"# A pandas Series with nullable Int32 dtype and missing values\n"
"pd.Series([1, 2, pd.NA], dtype=\"Int32\")\n"
"\n"
"# A pandas Series using a PyArrow-backed float64 dtype\n"
"pd.Series([1, 2, 3], dtype=\"float64[pyarrow]\")\n"
"\n"
"# A PyArrow array with dtype uint8\n"
"pa.array([1, 2, 3], type=pa.uint8())\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:69
msgid "String Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:71
msgid ""
"In addition to Python's built-in {class}`str` type, PyGMT also supports the "
"following string dtypes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:74
msgid ""
"NumPy: {class}`numpy.str_` or fixed-width Unicode string dtype (e.g., "
"``\"U10\"``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:75
msgid ""
"pandas: {class}`pandas.StringDtype`, with different storage backends, "
"including `string[python]` and `string[pyarrow]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:77
msgid ""
"PyArrow: {func}`pyarrow.string`/{func}`pyarrow.utf8`, {func}`pyarrow."
"large_string`/{func}`pyarrow.large_utf8`, and {func}`pyarrow.string_view`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:82
msgid "Examples of string arrays supported by PyGMT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:84
msgid ""
"# A list of strings\n"
"[\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n"
"\n"
"# A NumPy string array\n"
"np.array([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"])\n"
"np.array([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], dtype=np.str_)\n"
"\n"
"# A pandas.Series string array\n"
"pd.Series([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], dtype=\"string\")\n"
"pd.Series([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], dtype=\"string[python]\")\n"
"pd.Series([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], dtype=\"string[pyarrow]\")\n"
"\n"
"# A PyArrow array with pyarrow.string dtype\n"
"pa.array([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"], type=pa.string())\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:102
msgid "Datetime Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:104
msgid "PyGMT supports a variety of datetime types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:106
msgid ""
"A list/tuple of elements in Python's built-in {class}`datetime.datetime` or "
"{class}`datetime.date`, datetime-like strings, or mixed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:108
msgid "NumPy arrays: {class}`numpy.datetime64` with various resolutions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:109
msgid ""
"pandas objects with {class}`numpy.datetime64`, {class}`pandas."
"DatetimeTZDtype`, {func}`pyarrow.timestamp` with various resolution and "
"timezone support, and pyarrow-backend dtypes like `date32[day][pyarrow]` and "
"`date64[ms][pyarrow]`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:112
msgid ""
"PyArrow: {func}`pyarrow.date32`, {func}`pyarrow.date64` and {func}`pyarrow."
"timestamp` with various resolutions and timezone support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:115
msgid "Timedelta Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:117
msgid ""
"PyGMT supports NumPy arrays with the {class}`numpy.timedelta64` dtype. "
"Timedelta values are passed to GMT as their underlying integer values, so "
"their unit determines the numeric scale. For example, a `timedelta64[D]` "
"array is interpreted as days, whereas a `timedelta64[s]` array is "
"interpreted as seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:122
msgid ""
"Timedelta values can also be used in sequence-valued parameters such as "
"``region``. The timedelta dtype does not, by itself, configure a GMT "
"relative-time axis; configure GMT time settings explicitly when a relative-"
"time axis is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:126
msgid "Unsupported Dtypes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:128
msgid ""
"The following dtypes are intentionally unsupported, and should be cast to an "
"appropriate supported dtype before passing to PyGMT:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:131
msgid ""
"Floating-point dtypes: `numpy.float16`, {func}`pyarrow.float16` and {class}"
"`numpy.longdouble`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:133
msgid ""
"Boolean dtypes: {class}`numpy.bool`, {class}`pandas.BooleanDtype` and {func}"
"`pyarrow.bool_`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:135
msgid "Complex dtypes: `numpy.complex64`, `numpy.complex128`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:136
msgid "{class}`numpy.bytes_` and {class}`numpy.void`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../techref/array_dtypes.md:138
msgid ""
"The {class}`numpy.object_` dtype is also not supported. PyGMT may convert "
"object arrays that can be interpreted as datetimes or text, but applications "
"should create arrays with an explicit supported dtype instead."
msgstr ""
